session Symmetric_Matrix_Spectra = "HOL-Analysis" +
  description "
    The spectral theory of real symmetric matrices that HOL-Analysis stops
    short of -- a calculus of trace, transpose and outer products (on
    HOL-Analysis's outer_prod), orthonormal families and the orthogonal
    projections onto them, positive semidefinite matrices, norm bounds from
    bounds on the quadratic form, Householder reflections and rotations, the
    spectral theorem, Ky Fan partial sums, the ordered eigenvalues as their
    differences, their Lipschitz dependence on the matrix, the Rayleigh
    bounds and the Courant-Fischer lower bound -- for anyone who
    constrains a matrix through its spectrum rather than through its
    entries.
  "
  options [document = pdf, document_output = "output"]
  theories
    Matrix_Algebra
    Outer_Products
    Orthonormal_Families
    Orthogonal_Projections
    Symmetric_Spectral
    Ky_Fan
    Eigenvalue_Continuity
    Eigenvalue_Bounds
    Householder_Rotation
  document_files
    "root.tex"
    "root.bib"
